#N canvas 20 20 660 540 10;
#N canvas 60 60 620 620 readme 0;
#X text 10 10 juno~ editor \; \; [junoedit <bus>] sends to [s <bus>] (the [r <bus>] in front of juno~) and reads outlet 3 of juno~ from [r <bus>-out]. In your own patch: [r j1] -> [juno~] -> outlet 3 -> [route float] -> right outlet -> [s j1-out] and [junoedit j1]. Every change (controller \, patch change \, messages \, SysEx) shows up here. \; \; Rows of 8: the rows are the pages of the controller layer [junocc] (page k on the controller = row k). Each cell: name and label \, slider and number box: the value as from a pot (0-127) \, the box right of it: the value as on the panel. Edits are heard at once. \; \; Rows 1 to 3 are the patch: the 16 sliders and 8 switches of a Juno-106 patch. sub is the level of the sub oscillator \, 0 is off. chorus I+II is the third mode of the Juno-60 \, a Juno-106 plays it as I. The SETUP row belongs to the instrument and is not stored in a patch: volume \, tune \, bend range \, octave \, and how much the velocity changes level and cutoff (0 = not at all \, as on the instrument). \; \; factory N: a factory preset (read only). 0 to 55 are the sounds of the Juno-60 \, after them come the Juno-106 banks (.syx) found next to juno~. user N: a slot of the user bank (0-55 \, shown as bank and number 11 to 78). reload: the same patch again \, edits dropped. init patch: a plain sawtooth to start from. \; \; store to N chooses a user slot \, save patch stores the playing patch there and writes junouser-bank.syx (next to juno~). load bank reads that file again \, write bank writes it without storing. \; \; send bank / send patch: the user bank or the playing patch as Juno-106 SysEx on the third outlet of juno~ (to [midiout]). A Juno-106 plays a patch it receives but does not store it by itself: after send bank it holds the last patch \, press WRITE on it to keep one. A patch that arrives at juno~ replaces the playing patch \, store it to keep it. \; \; SysEx for every change: juno~ then behaves like a Juno-106 and sends a parameter message for every edit and the patch on every patch change \, for editors and for a Juno-106 that should follow. Off by default. \; \; MIDI in: receive channel of juno~ for raw MIDI \, note lists and SysEx \, 0 = all. out: the channel of the controller feedback and of SysEx. The controller layer follows both., f 92;
